{%- set faqs = [
  ["Why is penetration testing important for businesses?", "Penetration testing helps identify security weaknesses before attackers exploit them. It supports risk reduction, data protection and stronger security controls while helping organizations understand how vulnerabilities could affect business operations."],
  ["What types of penetration testing does CipherTrivia provide?", "CipherTrivia offers penetration testing across web applications, mobile applications, APIs, internal and external networks, cloud environments and wireless networks, depending on the agreed testing scope and service availability."],
  ["How often should penetration testing be performed?", "Businesses commonly conduct penetration testing annually and after significant changes to applications, infrastructure or security controls. Testing may also be required following major releases, security incidents or compliance reviews."],
  ["What is the difference between vulnerability assessment and penetration testing?", "A vulnerability assessment identifies and evaluates potential security weaknesses. Penetration testing goes further by safely validating selected vulnerabilities to understand how they could be exploited and what impact they may have."],
  ["How long does a penetration testing engagement take?", "The timeline depends on the number of systems, application complexity, testing scope and environment size. A focused assessment may take a few days, while larger applications or infrastructure environments may require several weeks."],
  ["What does a penetration testing report include?", "A penetration testing report typically includes identified vulnerabilities, severity ratings, supporting evidence, potential business impact and recommended fixes. Depending on the engagement, it may also include an executive summary, attack path analysis and retesting results."],
  ["Does penetration testing affect website or application performance?", "Penetration testing is planned to minimize disruption through agreed testing boundaries and controlled methods. Some tests can affect system availability, so testing conditions, exclusions and safeguards should be established before work begins."],
  ["Can penetration testing help with compliance requirements?", "Yes. Penetration testing can support security and compliance activities associated with standards such as PCI DSS, ISO 27001 and SOC 2, where relevant. Testing alone does not guarantee certification or compliance, but its findings can help address security control gaps."],
  ["What happens after vulnerabilities are identified?", "The testing team documents the findings and provides remediation recommendations based on risk and severity. Your technical team can then implement fixes, followed by retesting where included in the engagement scope to verify whether the issues have been resolved."],
  ["What is included in cloud penetration testing?", "Cloud penetration testing examines authorized cloud environments such as AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud for weaknesses involving access permissions, exposed resources, insecure configurations and potential unauthorized access paths."],
  ["How can we get started with CipherTrivia's penetration testing services?", "Contact CipherTrivia to discuss your applications, infrastructure, security concerns and testing objectives. Based on your requirements, the assessment scope can be defined to identify relevant security risks and provide actionable remediation guidance."]
] %}

