<section class="section section--paper" id="types" aria-labelledby="s2-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="shead">
      <div class="shead__meta"></div>
      <div class="shead__body">
        <h2 class="shead__title rv" id="s2-title">Types of Penetration Testing Services We Provide</h2>
        <p class="shead__lede rv" style="--d:1">CipherTrivia offers penetration testing services to help organizations identify exploitable security weaknesses across applications, APIs, networks and cloud infrastructure. Our assessments simulate realistic attack scenarios within an authorized scope to evaluate security controls, validate vulnerabilities and provide practical remediation recommendations.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="ledger">
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("browser") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Web Application Penetration Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We assess web applications for vulnerabilities involving authentication, session management, access controls, input validation and business logic. Testing helps identify weaknesses that could expose sensitive information or allow unauthorized actions.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("mobile") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Mobile Application Penetration Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We evaluate Android and iOS applications for insecure data storage, weak authentication, improper permissions, insecure API communication and other mobile-specific security risks.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("api") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">API Penetration Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Our API testing examines authentication, authorization, object-level access controls, rate limiting and data exposure. It helps identify weaknesses in REST and GraphQL APIs that could allow unauthorized access or misuse of business functionality.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:3">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("network") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Network Penetration Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We assess internal and external networks for exposed services, insecure configurations, weak access controls and exploitable vulnerabilities. Testing helps organizations understand potential attack paths across their network infrastructure.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("cloud-lock") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Cloud Penetration Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We assess in-scope cloud environments hosted on AWS, Microsoft Azure or Google Cloud for exploitable configuration weaknesses, excessive permissions, exposed services and potential paths to unauthorized resource access.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("wifi") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Wireless Network Penetration Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We evaluate authorized wireless networks for weak encryption, insecure configurations, authentication weaknesses and potential unauthorized access to identify risks affecting wireless connectivity.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("target") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Red Team Assessment</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We simulate defined attacker objectives to evaluate how effectively security controls detect and respond to realistic attack techniques. Depending on the engagement scope, testing may cover technology, detection capabilities and incident response processes.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:3">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("directory") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Active Directory &amp; Internal Security Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We examine identity infrastructure, privilege assignments, authentication policies and internal attack paths to identify weaknesses that could allow an attacker to escalate privileges or move across systems.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

