          <h3 class="explorer__name">Web Application Penetration Testing</h3>
          <p class="explorer__text">We test web applications for authentication bypass, session hijacking, SQL injection, cross-site scripting (XSS), server-side request forgery (SSRF) and insecure access controls. Assessments reference relevant OWASP Top 10 risks and applicable application security testing standards.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="explorer__item rv" data-explorer-item>
          <img class="explorer__inline" src="/assets/images/penetration-testing/cover-api.webp" width="1200" height="1500" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <h3 class="explorer__name">API Penetration Testing (REST &amp; GraphQL)</h3>
          <p class="explorer__text">Our API penetration testing services evaluate authentication and authorization controls, broken object-level authorization (BOLA), excessive data exposure, injection vulnerabilities and rate-limit weaknesses. Testing helps identify API security gaps that could expose sensitive data or permit unauthorized operations.</p>
