<section class="section section--stone" aria-labelledby="s5-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="shead">
      <div class="shead__meta"></div>
      <div class="shead__body">
        <h2 class="shead__title rv" id="s5-title">Attack Scenarios Our Penetration Testing Services Simulate</h2>
        <p class="shead__lede rv" style="--d:1">CipherTrivia's penetration testing services simulate realistic cyberattacks within an authorized testing scope to identify exploitable weaknesses and evaluate how existing security controls respond to threats. These assessments help organizations understand potential attack paths, measure security gaps and prioritize remediation before vulnerabilities are exploited by malicious actors.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="triggers">
      <div class="trigger rv">
        <span class="trigger__ico">{{ icon("unlock", "lg") }}</span>
        <h3 class="trigger__title">Unauthorized Access &amp; Authentication Bypass</h3>
        <p class="trigger__text">We test authentication mechanisms, session management and access controls to identify weaknesses that could allow attackers to bypass login protections, hijack sessions or access restricted resources.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trigger rv">
        <span class="trigger__ico">{{ icon("escalate", "lg") }}</span>
        <h3 class="trigger__title">Privilege Escalation</h3>
        <p class="trigger__text">Our testing examines whether weaknesses in user permissions, system configurations or identity controls could allow a low-privileged user to gain unauthorized administrative access to critical systems.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trigger rv">
        <span class="trigger__ico">{{ icon("database", "lg") }}</span>
        <h3 class="trigger__title">Sensitive Data Exposure</h3>
        <p class="trigger__text">We assess applications, APIs, databases and cloud storage for vulnerabilities that could expose confidential business information, customer records, credentials or personal data to unauthorized users.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trigger rv">
        <span class="trigger__ico">{{ icon("syringe", "lg") }}</span>
        <h3 class="trigger__title">Injection Attacks &amp; Remote Code Execution</h3>
        <p class="trigger__text">We test for vulnerabilities such as SQL injection, command injection and cross-site scripting (XSS) to determine whether untrusted input could compromise application functionality, expose data or allow unauthorized actions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trigger rv">
        <span class="trigger__ico">{{ icon("lateral", "lg") }}</span>
        <h3 class="trigger__title">Lateral Movement &amp; Internal Network Compromise</h3>
        <p class="trigger__text">We simulate attack paths within authorized internal environments to identify how compromised credentials or vulnerable systems could allow attackers to move between devices, access additional resources or reach critical infrastructure.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trigger rv">
        <span class="trigger__ico">{{ icon("cloud-alert", "lg") }}</span>
        <h3 class="trigger__title">Cloud Misconfiguration Exploitation</h3>
        <p class="trigger__text">We evaluate cloud environments for excessive permissions, exposed storage, insecure identity policies and misconfigured services that could create opportunities for unauthorized access or compromise of cloud resources.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trigger rv">
        <span class="trigger__ico">{{ icon("code", "lg") }}</span>
        <h3 class="trigger__title">API Abuse &amp; Business Logic Exploitation</h3>
        <p class="trigger__text">We examine APIs and application workflows for broken access controls, parameter manipulation, excessive data exposure and business logic flaws that could allow unauthorized transactions or misuse of application functionality.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trigger rv">
        <span class="trigger__ico">{{ icon("eye-off", "lg") }}</span>
        <h3 class="trigger__title">Security Control &amp; Detection Gaps</h3>
        <p class="trigger__text">We evaluate how existing security controls respond to approved attack simulations and identify gaps in logging, monitoring, alerting and incident response that may delay threat detection.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

